# Converted to the revised ten-section template (plus section 11); content and tables carried from the previous version.
BOOK = '1 Thessalonians'
TESTAMENT = 'New Testament'
GENRE = 'letters'
SUBTITLE = 'Faith, Love, Hope, and the Lord’s Coming for Us'
SECTIONS = [(1, 'Book Setting & Program Identity', [('p', 'This section introduces you to the book by explaining who wrote it, who received it, and what was happening when it was written. It also shows you which of God’s programs the book belongs to — Israel’s prophetic program or the Body of Christ’s mystery program. Knowing the setting and the program identity helps you read the book in its proper context and understand how its teachings fit into the larger story of Scripture.'), ('p', '1 Thessalonians is a letter from Paul, Silvanus and Timotheus “unto the church of the Thessalonians which is in God the Father and in the Lord Jesus Christ” (1 Thess. 1:1). Paul recalls how the gospel came to them, how they turned from idols, and how he cared for them. He then gives instruction on holy living, comfort about those who sleep, and the day of the Lord.'), ('box', 'Program Identity:', '1 Thessalonians is addressed to a young church of believers. It sets the hope of those in Christ beside the day of the Lord, and it says that God has not appointed them to wrath (1 Thess. 5:9). This reading rests on the letter’s own audience markers and setting.')]),
(2, 'Narrative Flow of 1 Thessalonians', [('p', 'This section gives you a simple walkthrough of how the book unfolds. Instead of diving into details right away, it shows the major movements in the letter — how Paul begins, how his instructions develop, and how the letter builds toward its close. Seeing the flow of the book helps you understand the big picture before you study the individual passages.'), ('h3', 'Movement 1 — The Gospel Received and the Work of Faith (Chs. 1–2)'), ('p', 'Paul gives thanks for their work of faith, labour of love, and patience of hope, recalls how they turned to God from idols, and describes his gentle care among them (1 Thess. 1:3, 9–10; 2:7–13).'), ('h3', 'Movement 2 — Timothy’s Report and Holy Living (Chs. 3–4:12)'), ('p', 'Paul sends Timothy, receives good news, and urges them to abound in love, to be sanctified, and to walk honestly (1 Thess. 3:1–6, 12; 4:1–12).'), ('h3', 'Movement 3 — The Hope and the Day of the Lord (4:13–5:11)'), ('p', 'Paul comforts them about those who sleep with the Lord’s descent from heaven, then writes of the day of the Lord coming as a thief (1 Thess. 4:13–18; 5:1–11).'), ('h3', 'Movement 4 — Closing Exhortations (5:12–28)'), ('p', 'Paul gives short commands for the church’s life and prays that they be sanctified wholly (1 Thess. 5:12–24).')]),
(3, 'Program Themes in 1 Thessalonians', [('p', 'This section highlights the major ideas Paul emphasizes in this book — the big doctrinal themes that shape how the Body of Christ should think and live. These themes are not verse-by-verse explanations; they are the book’s main emphases, the repeated ideas Paul wants believers to carry forward. Seeing these themes together helps you understand the book’s message before you look at the individual truths in the tables.'), ('ol', ['<b>The Work of Faith</b> — Paul remembers their “work of faith, and labour of love, and patience of hope” (1 Thess. 1:3).', '<b>Turning to God</b> — They turned to God from idols “to serve the living and true God” (1 Thess. 1:9).', '<b>The Word Received</b> — They received the word “not as the word of men, but as it is in truth, the word of God” (1 Thess. 2:13).', '<b>Comfort in Death</b> — Paul does not want them ignorant concerning those who sleep (1 Thess. 4:13).', '<b>Not Appointed to Wrath</b> — “God hath not appointed us to wrath, but to obtain salvation by our Lord Jesus Christ” (1 Thess. 5:9).'])]),
(4, 'Christ in 1 Thessalonians', [('p', 'This section gathers what the letter teaches about Christ — who He is, what He has done, and how Paul presents Him to the church. These statements help you see the book’s Christ-centered focus before you study the doctrinal truths in detail. By collecting these verses together, you get a clear picture of how 1 Thessalonians lifts up Christ.'), ('ol', ['<b>God’s Son from Heaven</b> — They wait for His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead, who delivered them from the wrath to come (1 Thess. 1:10).', '<b>The Lord Who Died and Rose</b> — “If we believe that Jesus died and rose again” (1 Thess. 4:14).', '<b>The Lord Himself</b> — “The Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout” (1 Thess. 4:16).', '<b>Who Died for Us</b> — Christ died for us, “that, whether we wake or sleep, we should live together with him” (1 Thess. 5:10).', '<b>Our Lord Jesus Christ</b> — Salvation is obtained by our Lord Jesus Christ (1 Thess. 5:9).'])]),
(5, 'The Church, the Law, and Israel in 1 Thessalonians', [('p', 'This section helps you see how 1 Thessalonians speaks about the church, the law, and Israel without mixing their programs. By gathering these points together, this section shows you how to read 1 Thessalonians in its own setting — as a Body-of-Christ letter — while recognizing what it says (and does not say) about Israel’s program.'), ('p', 'The letter sets the hope of believers beside the day of the Lord:'), ('ul', ['The letter names the Lord’s descent from heaven, the dead in Christ rising first, and the living being caught up together with them (1 Thess. 4:16–17).', 'The day of the Lord is set beside this hope, and Paul tells the church it is not appointed to wrath (1 Thess. 5:2, 9).', 'The letter speaks of Jews who killed the Lord Jesus and of wrath come upon them (1 Thess. 2:14–16). The study reports the text as written.', 'The letter does not make the church a party to any Israelite covenant.']), ('p', 'This reading rests on the letter’s own audience markers and setting.')]),
(6, 'Body-of-Christ Distinctions', [('p', 'This section highlights the teachings in 1 Thessalonians that belong uniquely to the Body of Christ — truths Paul gives to the church in this present age. By gathering these together, this section helps you see how 1 Thessalonians contributes to the doctrine and order of the Body of Christ without borrowing from Israel’s prophetic program.'), ('p', '1 Thessalonians teaches the standing and hope of the church in Christ:'), ('ul', ['a church in God the Father and in the Lord Jesus Christ', 'the Lord’s descent and the gathering of the dead and living in Christ (1 Thess. 4:16–17)', 'not appointed to wrath but to salvation (1 Thess. 5:9)', 'sanctification, love and quiet living (1 Thess. 4:3, 9–11)', 'comfort one toward another with these words (1 Thess. 4:18)']), ('p', 'It does not set a date for the Lord’s coming, and it says that the times and seasons are not written to them (1 Thess. 5:1).')]),
(7, 'Truths Table: What 1 Thessalonians Says', [('p', 'This table gathers the key statements, instructions, and teachings in 1 Thessalonians and shows which ones belong to the Body of Christ. Each row lists a truth from the letter, explains what it says, and identifies its program identity based on Paul’s audience and setting. This helps you see, at a glance, what 1 Thessalonians teaches directly to the church today and keeps those truths separate from universal principles or reports that apply more broadly.'), ('p', 'Program Identity shows where a truth belongs. “Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth” marks a statement, command, warning or instruction given to the Body of Christ through Paul.'), ('table', ['Category', 'Truth Revealed in 1 Thessalonians', 'Program Identity', 'Scripture'], [['Turning to God', 'They turned from idols to serve the living and true God.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 1:9'], ['The Hope', 'The Lord himself shall descend from heaven; the dead in Christ rise first.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 4:16'], ['Caught Up', 'The living are caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord in the air.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 4:17'], ['Not Appointed to Wrath', 'God hath not appointed us to wrath.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 5:9'], ['Sanctification', 'This is the will of God, even your sanctification.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 4:3'], ['The Day of the Lord', 'It so cometh as a thief in the night.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 5:2'], ['Jews and Wrath', 'Wrath is come upon them to the uttermost.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 2:14–16'], ['Wake or Sleep', 'Whether we wake or sleep, we should live together with Christ.', 'Body of Christ (Pauline) Truth', '1 Thess. 5:10']], [20, 36, 26, 18])]),
(8, 'Universal Truths Table (All People, All Time)', [('p', 'This table gathers the truths in 1 Thessalonians that apply to everyone, not just the Body of Christ. These are principles rooted in God’s character — things that hold true across all programs and all ages. By separating these universal truths from Paul’s program-specific instructions, this section helps you see what 1 Thessalonians teaches all believers everywhere and what it teaches the church in its own setting.'), ('table', ['Universal Truth', 'Description', 'Scripture'], [['Love One Another', 'Increase and abound in love one toward another.', '1 Thess. 3:12'], ['Quiet Living', 'Study to be quiet, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands.', '1 Thess. 4:11'], ['Comfort One Another', 'Comfort one another with these words.', '1 Thess. 4:18'], ['Rejoice Evermore', 'Rejoice evermore.', '1 Thess. 5:16'], ['Pray Without Ceasing', 'Pray without ceasing.', '1 Thess. 5:17'], ['Give Thanks', 'In every thing give thanks.', '1 Thess. 5:18'], ['Prove All Things', 'Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.', '1 Thess. 5:21'], ['Abstain from Evil', 'Abstain from all appearance of evil.', '1 Thess. 5:22']], [30, 46, 24])]),
(9, 'Program-Safe Application Grid', [('p', 'This section shows how to apply the teachings of 1 Thessalonians without mixing programs. The applications come directly from Paul’s instructions to the Body of Christ and from the universal truths that apply to everyone. By keeping the applications tied to what the letter actually says — and not borrowing commands from Israel’s covenants or prophetic program — this grid helps you respond to 1 Thessalonians in a way that is faithful to its setting, clear, and safe.'), ('ol', ['<b>Work in faith and love</b> — Keep the work of faith and labour of love (1 Thess. 1:3).', '<b>Serve the living God</b> — Turn from idols to serve Him (1 Thess. 1:9).', '<b>Walk in holiness</b> — Live in sanctification (1 Thess. 4:3–7).', '<b>Comfort one another</b> — Use the words about the Lord’s coming for comfort (1 Thess. 4:18).', '<b>Be watchful and sober</b> — Put on faith and love and the hope of salvation (1 Thess. 5:6–8).', '<b>Respect those who labour</b> — Know them that labour among you (1 Thess. 5:12–13).', '<b>Rejoice, pray, give thanks</b> — Practice the short commands of 5:16–18.', '<b>Hold fast the good</b> — Prove all things (1 Thess. 5:21).'])]),
(10, 'Teaching Outline for 1 Thessalonians', [('p', 'This outline gives you a teacher-ready structure for presenting the book. It follows the narrative movements and highlights the major themes, making it easy to teach 1 Thessalonians in classes, small groups, or personal study.'), ('olr', ['The Gospel Received (Ch. 1) — Their work of faith and turning to God. <i>(1 Thess. 1:3, 9–10)</i>', 'Paul’s Care (Ch. 2) — The word received and Paul’s gentle labour. <i>(1 Thess. 2:7–13)</i>', 'Timothy’s Report (Ch. 3) — Faith and love established. <i>(1 Thess. 3:6–13)</i>', 'Walking to Please God (4:1–12) — Sanctification, love, quiet living. <i>(1 Thess. 4:3, 9–11)</i>', 'The Hope of Those Who Sleep (4:13–18) — The Lord’s descent and comfort. <i>(1 Thess. 4:13–18)</i>', 'The Day of the Lord (5:1–11) — Not appointed to wrath. <i>(1 Thess. 5:2, 9)</i>', 'Closing Commands (5:12–28) — Short exhortations and prayer. <i>(1 Thess. 5:16–24)</i>'])]),
(11, 'Companion Usage and Study Suggestions', [('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Personal Study'), ('p', 'This Companion is designed to walk alongside you as you read 1 Thessalonians, helping you see both what the letter says to believers and the timeless truths rooted in God’s character. Use it slowly, chapter by chapter, letting the narrative movements, themes, and truths deepen your understanding. The Program-Safe Applications draw only on what 1 Thessalonians itself says, so your response stays tied to the text.'), ('h3', 'How to Use This Companion in Small Groups or Classes'), ('p', 'This Companion provides a clear, structured framework that makes teaching 1 Thessalonians simple and accessible. Each section gives you ready-to-use material: narrative movements for overview, program themes for doctrinal clarity, universal truths for discussion, and a pastoral teaching outline for weekly lessons. Use the tables to help your group see what the letter states and what it leaves unsaid, and use the Program-Safe Application Grid to foster meaningful, Christ-centered conversation.'), ('h3', 'How This Companion Fits Within the Acts Overlap Theology Series'), ('p', 'This Companion is part of a larger series designed to help believers read every book of Scripture without blurring God’s prophetic program for Israel and His mystery program for the Body of Christ. Within the Acts Overlap framework, 1 Thessalonians was written during the overlap to a church of believers. This Companion shows you how to read its hope and its report on the day of the Lord each in its own setting while drawing out the principles that apply to all believers.')])]

# Place in God's Storyline (Master Standard v1.155): last item of Section 1
from storyline import S as _STORY
SECTIONS[0][2].append(('p', '<b>Place in God’s Storyline.</b> ' + _STORY['1thessalonians'][1]))
